From 72137c6c6eda86325ab4a92dc44e0581c8d55840 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Belfry <belfry@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:55:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Belfry: the village space joins itself; sign-in first, no
 sign-up

In platform mode the space is every participant's (the relay has them as a member already),
so it is joined without the dialog, which stays as the fallback when access fails. Without a
push server there is no notifications toggle. The landing page offers "Sign in with Open
Source Village" first and "Use your own Nostr signer" below it; instead of creating an
account (accounts come with a pass), "No pass yet? Ask for an invite" links to the start page.
